      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "Let me show you the picture that quietly ruins most people's progress. Here is the most important chart in the book, and almost nobody draws it right. We expect our effort to pay off in a straight diagonal line. We expect that if we put in the work, the results should arrive on schedule, evenly, day by day. Clear calls this expectation the great lie of self improvement, because reality does not work that way at all. Your real progress hides for a long time, flat and frustrating, and then it erupts all at once.",
